Cell.</source> <volume>10</volume>:<fpage>9</fpage>&#x02013;22.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9880323</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal">Braren, R., H. Hu, Y.H. Kim, H.E. Beggs, L.F. Reichardt, and R. Wang. <year>2006</year>. Endothelial FAK is essential for vascular network stability, cell survival, and lamellipodial formation. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>172</volume>:<fpage>151</fpage>&#x02013;162.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16391003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Byers, H.R., G.E. White, and K. Fujiwara. <year>1984</year>. Organization and function of stress fibers in cells in vitro and in situ. A review. <source>Cell Muscle Motil.</source> <volume>5</volume>:<fpage>83</fpage>&#x02013;137.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6367964</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Carbajal, J.M., and R.C. Schaeffer Jr. <year>1999</year>. RhoA inactivation enhances endothelial barrier function. <source>Am. J. Physiol.</source> <volume>277</volume>:<fpage>C955</fpage>&#x02013;C964.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10564088</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Carmeliet, P., M.G. Lampugnani, L. Moons, F. Breviario, V. Compernolle, F. Bono, G. Balconi, R. Spagnuolo, B. Oostuyse, M. Dewerchin, et al. <year>1999</year>. Targeted deficiency or cytosolic truncation of the VE-cadherin gene in mice impairs VEGF-mediated endothelial survival and angiogenesis. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>98</volume>:<fpage>147</fpage>&#x02013;157.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10428027</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Cattelino, A., S. Liebner, R. Gallini, A. Zanetti, G. Balconi, A. Corsi, P. Bianco, H. Wolburg, R. Moore, B. Oreda, et al. <year>2003</year>. The conditional inactivation of the &#x003b2;-catenin gene in endothelial cells causes a defective vascular pattern and increased vascular fragility. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>162</volume>:<fpage>1111</fpage>&#x02013;1122.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12975353</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Comerford, K.M., D.W. Lawrence, K. Synnestvedt, B.P. Levi, and S.P. Colgan. <year>2002</year>. Role of vasodilator-stimulated phosphoprotein in PKA-induced changes in endothelial junctional permeability. <source>FASEB J.</source> <volume>16</volume>:<fpage>583</fpage>&#x02013;585.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11919161</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Corada, M., M. Mariotti, G. Thurston, K. Smith, R. Kunkel, M. Brockhaus, M.G. Lampugnani, I. Martin-Padura, A. Stoppacciaro, L. Ruco, et al. <year>1999</year>. Vascular endothelial-cadherin is an important determinant of microvascular integrity in vivo. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>96</volume>:<fpage>9815</fpage>&#x02013;9820.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10449777</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Dejana, E., G. Bazzoni, and M.G. Lampugnani. <year>1999</year>. Vascular endothelial (VE)-cadherin: only an intercellular glue? <source>Exp. Cell Res.</source> <volume>252</volume>:<fpage>13</fpage>&#x02013;19.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10502395</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Drenckhahn, D., and J. Wagner. <year>1986</year>. Stress fibers in the splenic sinus endothelium in situ: molecular structure, relationship to the extracellular matrix, and contractility. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>102</volume>:<fpage>1738</fpage>&#x02013;1747.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3084499</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Dudek, S.M., J.R. Jacobson, E.T. Chiang, K.G. Birukov, P. Wang, X. Zhan, and J.G. Garcia. <year>2004</year>. Pulmonary endothelial cell barrier enhancement by sphingosine 1-phosphate: roles for cortactin and myosin light chain kinase. <source>J. Biol. Chem.